The time complexity (in terms of the number of calls to `work()`) of the following code, for an integer $n\ge1$, is

```c
for (i = 1; i < n; i = i * 2)
    for (j = 0; j < i; j++)
        work();
```

The following function is called as `g(8)`. How many calls to `g` are made in total, including the initial call?

```python
def g(n):
    if n <= 1:
        return 1
    return g(n - 1) + g(n // 2)
```
